{
  "_readme": "Add or change queries here, then relaunch Aducks. Structure: categories -> queries -> lookups. The UI asks, in order: (1) the Category, (2) the Query, (3) the Lookup, (4) the Value. The 4 step labels are set in settings.json ('Labels'). Steps hide automatically: step 3 (the Lookup) is hidden when a query has only ONE lookup; step 4 (the Value box) is hidden when the lookup's Url has NO {value} - that is how you say 'this query needs no input' (e.g. 'me'). Each Lookup holds a Graph Url; {value} is replaced by the user's input (URL-encoded automatically); relative Urls are added to the Graph v1.0 base, full https:// Urls are used as-is. Optional per-lookup fields: 'ValueLabel' overrides the label above the value box; 'ValueHint' is grey placeholder text shown inside the box (give every {value} lookup one - show a real example value, no 'e.g.' prefix). Props are the return fields the user can tick (a checkable multi-select); with none ticked the query is sent with no $select and Graph returns its default fields. Paste any Graph endpoint URL here - no code changes. Chained lookups: instead of 'Url', a lookup may have 'Chain' - an array of steps [{Url, Extract}, ...] run in order. Step 1's {value} is the user's input; each later step's {value} is the previous step's 'Extract' path into its JSON result (e.g. 'value[0].id'). The last step's result is shown. Example: find a group's members by name - [{'Url':\"groups?$filter=displayName eq '{value}'\",'Extract':'value[0].id'},{'Url':'groups/{value}/members'}].",
